                    <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><a href="#cas-method"
                            style="color: var(--primary); text-decoration: none;">4. The CAS Method Explained</a></li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><a href="#step-by-step"
                            style="color: var(--primary); text-decoration: none;">5. Step-by-Step Guide: Arthavi</a>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><a href="#faqs"
                            style="color: var(--primary); text-decoration: none;">6. Frequently Asked Questions
                            (FAQs)</a></li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div id="wealth-fragmentation"
                style="margin: 3rem 0; padding: 2rem; background: var(--bg-surface); border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
                <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">The Problem: "Wealth Fragmentation"</h2>
                <p>As you grow your wealth, your investments naturally scatter. You might have:</p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    <li><strong>Stocks</strong> in a Demat account (e.g., Zerodha, Angel One).</li>
                    <li><strong>Mutual Funds</strong> in a different app (e.g., Groww, Coin) or physical folios.</li>
                    <li><strong>Gold/SGBs</strong> in a bank account.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>This fragmentation leads to three major issues:</p>
                <ol>
                    <li><strong>No True Net Worth:</strong> You never know <em>exactly</em> how much you have at any
                        given second.</li>
                    <li><strong>Hidden Overlap:</strong> You might own HDFC Bank via direct stock AND via three
                        different mutual funds without realizing it.</li>
                    <li><strong>XIRR Blindspots:</strong> Brokerage apps show simple returns (Absolute %), which hides
                        the impact of time on your SIPs. You need <a href="#" style="color: var(--primary);">XIRR
                            (Extended Internal Rate of Return)</a> to know your real performance.</li>
                </ol>
            </div>

            <h2 id="best-tools-india">Best Tools to Track Portfolio in India (2026)</h2>
            <p>If you're wondering what the best apps to track your portfolio are, here is a breakdown of the top tools
                available for Indian investors:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Arthavi:</strong> Best for privacy-conscious investors. Uses local CAS parsing instead of
                    email reading. It offers advanced XIRR and has zero ads.</li>
                <li><strong>INDmoney:</strong> Popular for complete automation and US stocks tracking. However, it
                    requires you to connect your Gmail account for auto-tracking, and it aggressively cross-sells loans
                    and other products.</li>
                <li><strong>Kuvera:</strong> Good for direct mutual fund investments. It also offers portfolio tracking
                    via email or CAS upload.</li>
                <li><strong>Groww & Zerodha:</strong> Excellent brokers, but they only provide a unified view of
                    investments made through their respective platforms. They are not true unified trackers.</li>
            </ul>

